> And are there any other general Rogue strategies that the more
> experienced members here can pass on?
	I'm not very experienced, but my first(and only) ascension was an 
orcish rogue, so I guess I can try.
	As I mentioned before, get a stack of good daggers, but don't make the 
mistake I made by waiting too long to use them. You can probably find 
about 20 normal uncursed daggers pretty easily, keep half of them in 
your blessed bag of holding(if you have one - if not, you need to get 
one) and the other half in your quiver. As you go on your way, collect 
elven daggers for a "dream stack" later on(take all elven daggers; even 
the cursed ones - just use cancellation when you need to
enchant them). Unless scrolls of enchant weapon are unusually abundant,
don't enchant your intermediate dagger stack too much.
	Don't write off Grayswandir as a primary weapon - it is not
intelligent, meaning that Chaotics can use it if they survive the blast.
When you get far enough, the blast is only a minor annoyance; on my
ascension, I used Magicbane throughout nearly the entire endgame. Also,
because you've used up skill slots on knife, if you intend to twoweapon,
a Grayswandir/silver saber combination could save you some slots you'd
normally use for long sword.
	There's also the more general advice; make sure you always have
reflection and magic resistance, and means of curing stoning, sliming,
as well as getting out of situations like cursed inventories and 
drowning in your main inventory(unless you have genocided the 
appropriate monsters). You should also try to be very fast and
unburdened. If you read spoilers; I highly recommend that
you read the Instadeath spoiler:
   http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/instadeath.html
This will help you get a sufficient level of paranoia :).

